Kipchoge-Style Finish as Kenyan Wins Budapest Marathon

Kenya's Samuel Kiprono won the Budapest Marathon on Sunday in 2:08:41, breaking the course record by 34 seconds. He pulled clear at 35 km and finished almost two minutes ahead of Ethiopia's Dawit Mekonnen.

In the women's race, Hungarian runner Anna Fazekas finished third in 2:29:52, her personal best and a national season's best. Temperatures of 9 degrees Celsius and little wind made for ideal conditions.

More than 14,000 runners took part. Organisers said next year's race would introduce an additional half-marathon wave to reduce congestion at the start.

